(vector (map (:adr/guardian-consent-check-design-7420 "minor-subject-guardian-consent-unresolved-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept in this fleet as a dedicated unconditional-evaluation CHECK FUNCTION (grep-verified -- the only prior hit was learning.facts's plain evidence-checklist STRING item 'guardian-consent-record', never a governor check), reusing the unconditional-evaluation DISCIPLINE (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix) for the 47th distinct grounding overall (continuing the count from holdco.governor/beneficial-ownership-verification-unresolved-violations at 46th), grounded directly in this blueprint's own Trust Control 'a consent/model-release gap forces a hold, not an override' and real image-rights law protecting minors"), (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492/6920/6611/7120/8620/8530/9200/7500/9603/9521/9321/8730/9102/9103/9602/9000/8890/8610/9311/8510/9412/6491/8720/8521/6619/3600/6190/3030/3830/7020/9420/9491/2610/3512/8810/8691/8569/6419/7310/7320/7210/7410/8710/8541/8690/9601/6420 ADR-0001s" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001")), (:adr/distinctive-check-7420 "model-release-coverage-insufficient? is the SEVENTH instance of this fleet's set-containment/subset check family (registrar/casework/secondary established the first three 'sufficiency' instances, consulting/congregation/design the fourth through sixth 'permission/boundary' instances), the FOURTH 'sufficiency' polarity instance -- an engagement's own recorded set of subjects requiring a model release must be fully covered by its own recorded set of subjects with a signed release"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607083500"), (:adr/deps-edn-current-coordinates-from-start-7420 "this build's deps.edn used the CURRENT io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph + langchain coordinates and :local/root paths from the very start (rather than the stale io.github.com-junkawasaki/langgraph-clj/langchain-clj coordinates every earlier sibling's deps.edn used), inheriting the fix holdco/6420's build discovered and documented -- see holdco/6420's own ADR-0001 for the full upstream-rename context (a repo transfer + rename, internal namespaces unchanged)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 62, :blueprint 22, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/test-status-7420 "30 tests / 134 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing (banking/6419-established discipline) -- 7 tests / 111 assertions, all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"7420\""), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607083500: `cloud-itonami-isic-7420` (photographic activities) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607083000 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9601`, washing and dry-cleaning)\n- ADR-2607083300 (`cloud-itonami-isic-6420`, activities of holding companies)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-7420/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph-clj` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-7420` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nphotographic activities: portrait, commercial and event photography,\nfilm processing, and related services. Like every prior vertical in\nthis fleet, the blueprint text alone is not an implementation — this\nADR records the governed-actor build that promotes `cloud-itonami-\nisic-7420` from `:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/\nindustry` registry, the forty-ninth vertical built outside\nADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-7420`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   photographic-studio operating model (engagement intake, shoot-plan\n   assessment, guardian-consent screening, final-image-set delivery)\n   but had no governed-actor implementation: no Store, no Governor,\n   no rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text names only ONE real-world act\n   (\"delivering/licensing a final image set to a client\") — this\n   build needed the single-actuation shape.\n3. Photography carries a genuine, real-world compliance concern\n   distinct from every prior sibling: delivering a commercial image\n   set requires every photographed subject who needs one to have\n   actually signed a model release — a coverage/sufficiency test,\n   distinct from `design`/7410's IP-licensing-scope concept.\n4. Photography of minors carries a heightened, distinctly regulated\n   consent concern (guardian consent) — this fleet already uses\n   \"guardian-consent-record\" as a generic evidence-checklist item\n   (`learning`/8569), but no prior sibling has built a DEDICATED\n   unconditional-evaluation check around it.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** Matching `leasing`/`underwriting`/\n   `testlab`/`clinic`/`veterinary`/`funeral`/`parksafety`/`salon`/\n   `entertainment`/`facility`/`consulting`/`advertising`/`polling`/\n   `research`/`design`/`sports`/`alliedhealth`'s single-actuation\n   shape, `high-stakes` is the one-member set `#{:actuation/deliver-\n   image-set}`.\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `engagement`. Four ops:\n   `:engagement/intake`, `:shootplan/verify`, `:consent/screen`,\n   `:actuation/deliver-image-set` (high-stakes).\n3. **`model-release-coverage-insufficient?` — the 7th set-\n   containment/subset instance, 4th \"sufficiency\" polarity.** Grep-\n   verified consistent with prior precedent. Following `registrar`/\n   `casework`/`secondary` (1st-3rd, \"sufficiency\"), `consulting`/\n   `congregation`/`design` (4th-6th, \"permission/boundary\"), this\n   recomputes `(not (set/subset? subjects-requiring-release subjects-\n   with-signed-release))` directly from the engagement's own recorded\n   fields. Gates only `:actuation/deliver-image-set`.\n4. **`minor-subject-guardian-consent-unresolved` — a genuinely new\n   check, the 47th unconditional-evaluation grounding.** Grep-verified\n   absent as a dedicated CHECK FUNCTION from every prior sibling\n   (only a plain evidence-checklist STRING item exists elsewhere).\n   Grounded in real image-rights law protecting minors (Germany's KUG\n   §22-23, US state right-of-publicity statutes) and this blueprint's\n   own Trust Control \"a consent/model-release gap forces a hold, not\n   an override.\" Gates `:consent/screen` and the actuation.\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:image-set-\n   delivered?` on the `engagement` record, never a single `:status`\n   value.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/photo/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor is\n   safely named `engagement` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3's `:auto` set is `{:engagement/\n   intake}` only; the actuation is permanently excluded from every\n   phase's `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** — this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** — the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Sixty-third actor in this fleet (62 implemented before this build).\n- Confirms the set-containment/subset check family generalizes to a\n  7th instance, and its \"sufficiency\" polarity to a 4th instance.\n- Establishes a genuinely NEW unconditional-evaluation-screening\n  concept (minor-subject-guardian-consent-unresolved) as a dedicated\n  check function, grep-verified previously present only as a generic\n  evidence-checklist string.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/photo/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 62 → 63, `:blueprint` 22 → 21,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 30 tests / 134 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing — 7 tests / 111 assertions,\n  all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"7420\".\n- This build's `deps.edn` used the CURRENT `kotoba-lang/langgraph`/\n  `langchain` coordinates from the start (see `holdco`/6420's own\n  ADR-0001 for the upstream-rename context this build inherited).\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| A dual-actuation shape | The blueprint's own text consistently names only ONE real-world act |\n| Reusing `design`/7410's IP-licensing-conflict concept for model-release coverage | Model-release coverage is a subject-consent concern (does the photographed person's own consent cover this use), genuinely distinct from a deliverable's own IP/licensing-clearance conflict |\n| Treating guardian-consent purely as a generic evidence-checklist item | This blueprint's own Trust Control text singles out \"a consent/model-release gap\" as forcing a hold -- a dedicated, unconditionally-evaluated check more precisely matches that emphasis |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7420/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7420/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7420/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"7420\"`)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 63, :blueprint 21, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 7420 (photographic activities) contributes a genuinely new dedicated check function (minor-subject-guardian-consent-unresolved) despite the underlying evidence-checklist concept already existing loosely elsewhere, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-7420 "tested via :consent/screen directly from the start (not via an actuation op against an unscreened engagement), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's, banking's, advertising's, polling's, research's, design's, nursing's, sports's, alliedhealth's, laundry's and holdco's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a thirty-seventh consecutive vertical"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-7420"), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-7420 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"7420\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding, confirmed by reading blueprint.edn before editing rather than assuming a fix was needed"), (:adr/single-actuation-7420 "matching leasing/underwriting/testlab/clinic/veterinary/funeral/parksafety/salon/entertainment/facility/consulting/advertising/polling/research/design/sports/alliedhealth's precedent, this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text names only ONE real-world act (delivering/licensing a final image set to a client), so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/deliver-image-set})"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-7420 (photographic activities) deepened to :implemented -- forty-ninth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-7420 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all"), (:adr/pattern-7420 "sealed PhotoOps-LLM + independent Shoot Delivery Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all sixty-two prior actors; FORTY-NINTH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420)")))